env-edit-shared-binary: cargo runs a binary's tests on parallel threads of one process, and testkit::env holds ENV_LOCK only against tests that also take it: a test that takes neither testkit::env nor testkit::env_read reads a home, PATH or config another thread has swapped, and fails in a way no rerun reproduces. In a single-file target, give every other test `let _env = testkit::env_read();` as its first line. A test that reaches an editing helper is covered by it and takes no env_read of its own: ENV_LOCK is not reentrant for a reader, so env_read held while a helper takes env deadlocks. In a multi-file target (`<crate>/tests/<dir>/…`) no module may edit: move the edit to its own `[[test]]` target.
test-id-unstamped: The id is stable with the test's intent: a rename or a move keeps it. A test rewritten to check something else gets a new id: delete its #[test_id] and run test-registry stamp --path <file> again. Never copy an id from another test.
spira-lint: RED — refused by env-edit-shared-binary (11), test-id-unstamped (40); errored: none
